Reading:
  * 'ms/token' falling as batch grows is unused GPU capacity being
    absorbed at no extra wall-clock cost. Once it flattens, the GPU is
    saturated and more work costs proportional time.
  * In sweep B, 'x canon ms' is what a wider model COSTS. A wider model
    can never make a run finish sooner -- it adds work to the same loop.
